Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:06.089
The level of discussion on The David Pakman
Show show lately has been very, very high

00:00:06.089 --> 00:00:07.299
and I mean a lot.

00:00:07.299 --> 00:00:08.299
Hi.

00:00:08.299 --> 00:00:09.390
To quote our president.

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:12.320
Join the discussion at David Pakman dot com
slash.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:13.350
Read it.

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:20.540
A user named J-P Denise's posted a very interesting
comparison of the policies of Bernie Sanders,

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:26.980
Joe Biden and Donald Trump to try to make
clear that there is really not very much in

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:31.320
common between Biden and Trump and quite a
bit in common between Joe Biden and Bernie

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.700
Sanders.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.680
And I think it's important for us to understand.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.840
I mean, listen, I don't think it's useful
to pretend that Joe Biden is something he

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:41.840
isn't.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:42.860
And that applies to both sides.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:44.470
Joe Biden is not Bernie Sanders.

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:45.840
Joe Biden is not a progressive.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:51.280
Joe Biden is not going to push for nearly
every policy that Bernie Sanders was pushing

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:52.280
for.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:55.470
But Joe Biden is way closer to Bernie than
he is to Donald Trump.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:01:00.260
And whether you look at the minimum wage,
paid family leave, Citizens United, the death

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:07.200
penalty, prison sentencing related to drugs,
abortion rights, capital gains taxes, wealth

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:15.280
taxes, the climate, nuclear power, you actually
see that Bernie and Trump are both no's, sort

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:16.280
of.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:17.280
And Biden is a yes.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.660
So in any case, that's not bragging about
Biden's position.

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:26.060
But the point is, if we say Biden's more like
Trump than Bernie, we are just very, very

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:27.060
wrong.

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:29.100
I want people deciding on the facts.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:34.619
If you think that we are better off with Trump
than Biden, then vote that way.

00:01:34.619 --> 00:01:43.060
But don't be tricked into making a move that
helps Trump because you incorrectly believe

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:50.020
that Biden and Trump share significant policy
when really the vast majority of the shared

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:53.960
policy is between Joe Biden and Bernie Sanders.

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:56.860
To different degrees on many issues.

00:01:56.860 --> 00:02:02.189
Decide however you want, but I want you to
decide with the facts, not with incorrect

00:02:02.189 --> 00:02:03.189
talking points.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:12.069
So a very good post by JP Denise's L Bun Zaino
posted Is David overusing the word weaponized?

00:02:12.069 --> 00:02:17.069
And a lot of people in the response is saying
this seems like a weird thing to be concerned

00:02:17.069 --> 00:02:19.590
about and it's an appropriate word to be using.

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:25.540
Yeah, my my use of the word weaponized has
definitely increased lately because we are

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:28.459
seeing so much weaponisation by the government.

00:02:28.459 --> 00:02:31.809
Donald Trump has webpack weaponized disinformation.

00:02:31.809 --> 00:02:34.860
Donald Trump has weaponized his delusions
of grandeur.

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:39.639
Donald Trump has weaponized his own and his
followers, ignorance and gullibility.

00:02:39.639 --> 00:02:45.019
We are seeing a level of weaponisation both
by Donald Trump and by right wing media that

00:02:45.019 --> 00:02:46.879
carries water for him.

00:02:46.879 --> 00:02:48.680
That is like nothing I've ever seen.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:50.359
And I was actually watching.

00:02:50.359 --> 00:02:54.810
I went on YouTube and I found some clips of
Fox News covering George W. Bush's presidency.

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:56.900
And of course, you know, it's the normal playbook.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:03:01.290
How do you support a standard Republican president
if you are standard right wing media?

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:06.319
And it almost seemed quaint compared to the
degree of weaponization that we are seeing

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:07.319
today.

00:03:07.319 --> 00:03:10.109
It's not a defensive George W. Bush and it's
not a defensive Fox News.

00:03:10.109 --> 00:03:19.620
It is merely a shocking realization I came
to of how far things have slid since the George

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:26.979
W. Bush Fox News era to the Trump Fox News
0a n phase in which we now find ourselves.

